@ 10.5.2 - Proto-Ongan to Onge
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Blevins, Juliette (2007), “A Long Lost Sister of Proto-Austronesian? Proto-Ongan, Mother of Jarawa and Onge of the Andaman Islands”. Oceanic Linguistics 46(I):154 – 198
	e > ə / _N, when unstressed (?)
	n > ŋ / _# (?)
	d > r / V_{V,#}
	{w,r} > ∅ / {a,e}_#
	∅ > e / C_#
	p > b
	aw > o
	e > {e,ə,o} / _V
	N > n / _{d,l}
	ɡd ɡl > d:[+long] l:[+long]